      <Placemark>
        <name>Coconut Garden Island Resort</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Contact No: 09185303903                             A resort off Port Barton which good in looking for a place to disconnect and relax, then this place is perfect. Booked through booking.com and most responsive on Facebook. <br>The room was some refreshing (mattresses, bed sheets, towels, mosquito nets) Power is only available during the three hours in the main restaurant in the evening during generator hours, and solar installations and kept their Starlink connection working during the day. <br>All food is made at the restaurant which is good enough with estimated food of Php250.00 - 400.00/meal. <br>Activities include snorkeling in the sea, swimming with the beautiful coral reef and kayaking, and estimate 300 to 400 per person per meal.  <br>id: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1602-C2185B</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value>Contact No: 09185303903                             A resort off Port Barton which good in looking for a place to disconnect and relax, then this place is perfect. Booked through booking.com and most responsive on Facebook. 
The room was some refreshing (mattresses, bed sheets, towels, mosquito nets) Power is only available during the three hours in the main restaurant in the evening during generator hours, and solar installations and kept their Starlink connection working during the day. 
All food is made at the restaurant which is good enough with estimated food of Php250.00 - 400.00/meal. 
Activities include snorkeling in the sea, swimming with the beautiful coral reef and kayaking, and estimate 300 to 400 per person per meal.  </value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="id">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
